-- E± pulls the attached vertex's Gram matrix back to λ± times the empty vertex's: λ₊ = 3/2 and λ₋ = 1 at spin ½.
-- With R±E± = 1 (`re-plus`, `re-minus`), E±† = λ± R± on the images, and tr(h h^{-1}) = Σ± w± R± E± = 2 with
-- w± = (d±1+1)/(d+1) = 3/2, ½; so the unitary holonomy's branches are Ê± = √(w±/λ±) E±, Ê±†Ê± = w±:
-- Ê₊ = E₊ and Ê₋ = E₋/√2, the branch probabilities per value of the open index ¾ and ¼, the dimensions 3 and 1 over 4.
attach-norm-check : Bool → SQ → Bool
attach-norm-check sp lam = rows-eq (gram-pull (gram (sp-ds sp 0 tet-ds)) (to-coords (vm-of (sp-ds sp 0 tet-ds) tet-ts) (e-map sp 0 tet-ds (inv-basis tet-ds))))
  (mat-scale lam (gram tet-ds))
